WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
- So before we go to break,

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.980
it's the first day of Black History Month

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:04.200
and you have a special connection

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.790
to the civil rights movement, right?

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:07.360
- Yes, absolutely.
- This is awesome, what is it?

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:09.370
- My grandfather, Reverend Hosea Williams,

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:11.690
the late Reverend Hosea Williams,

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.620
he worked, there's a picture right there

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.660
with Dr. Martin Luther King.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:16.493
- [Kelly Clarkson] Wow.

00:00:16.493 --> 00:00:17.340
- He was his right-hand man.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.530
He used to call my grandfather
the bull in the China cabinet

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:23.020
because he was the one when
they went to go marching,

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:24.174
he would get everybody rallied up.

00:00:24.174 --> 00:00:25.007
- [Kelly Clarkson] Yes.

00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:27.470
And energized and ready for the march,

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.940
and the purpose of the march.

00:00:28.940 --> 00:00:31.100
And so my grandfather's legacy

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.950
is that he was a civil rights activist

00:00:32.950 --> 00:00:35.680
and my family still
runs our family charity,

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.280
it's called 4hosea.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.230
- That's so cool.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.063
- [Porsha Williams] Yeah.

00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:40.030
- That's an amazing connection.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:40.880
- Like especially around
- Absolutely.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:43.170
this time like reminded
every year what your family,

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.225
those are amazing footprints

00:00:44.225 --> 00:00:45.080
to leave behind.
- Absolutely,

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.270
and you know Black History Month

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.890
is a month for us to really celebrate

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.420
who we are and our ancestors before us.

00:00:50.420 --> 00:00:52.960
So being able to educate the youth

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.260
and myself even more about
so many positive black people

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:59.210
who have been gone before
us and their footprints,

00:00:59.210 --> 00:01:01.985
we are now walking in is
such a powerful thing to do.

00:01:01.985 --> 00:01:03.680
- And even if you're not black,

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.310
it's an amazing time for everybody

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:07.660
to learn about something
maybe you didn't know.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.420
- And highlight the black experience.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.320
So black businesses, et cetera.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:13.320
Just lets everybody be black this month.

